# Rebuild dist-file after fixes

When you finish a **code fix or feature** that changes the runnable app (anything under `src/`, `index.html`, Vite configs, or assets that ship in the build), run:

```bash
npm run build:dist-file
```

Do this in the same turn as the fix — do not wait for the user to ask. Mention briefly that `dist-file` was rebuilt.

## Skip when

- Changes are docs/rules/tests-only and do not affect the built app
- The user explicitly says not to rebuild
- You only inspected code and made no edits

## Note

Publishing to **gh-pages** stays gated on commit+push (see `publish-gh-pages` rule). Rebuilding `dist-file` locally does not push Pages.
